    <briefdescription>
<para>Decides when queried data is worth a hover index. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A scan answers a query on any data at the cost of a pass over it. An index answers almost for free, but must be rebuilt after every data change. Queries therefore scan until the scans since the last data change have cost as much as a build would. That keeps the total within about twice the cheaper choice, whether the data changes every frame or never. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
